WEBVTT

00:00:00.627 --> 00:00:02.426
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you have any phobias?

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:05.628
<v><b>Jo:</b></v> Yes, I’m very scared of spiders.

00:00:06.181 --> 00:00:09.429
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> And how long have you had this phobia?

00:00:10.021 --> 00:00:14.907
<v><b>Jo:</b></v> I’ve had it since I was a child, so for more than 40 years.

00:00:15.385 --> 00:00:18.117
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Did something happen to start the phobia?

00:00:18.812 --> 00:00:24.036
<v><b>Jo:</b></v> Um well, not really, I’ve always been a bit afraid of spiders,

00:00:24.226 --> 00:00:28.452
maybe because my sisters used to chase me with them when I was a child,

00:00:28.819 --> 00:00:32.225
and I think as I got older, my fear got worse.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:38.281
But then something happened when I was in my 20s that made me think I had a real problem.

00:00:38.821 --> 00:00:44.890
I was in the car with my boyfriend, he was driving, and the road was very busy,

00:00:45.178 --> 00:00:50.264
and suddenly I saw a huge spider on the floor of the car, next to my foot.

00:00:50.456 --> 00:00:57.386
I was terrified, and my instinct was to try to get away from the spider as quickly as possible,

00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:01.087
so I opened my door, while he was still driving.

00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:03.257
It was really dangerous.

00:01:03.621 --> 00:01:07.463
Luckily he managed to stop and nothing happened,

00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:11.786
but I knew then that I had to do something about my phobia,

00:01:12.076 --> 00:01:15.857
 have some therapy, you know, get some professional help.

00:01:16.516 --> 00:01:18.662
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> What kind of therapy did you have?

00:01:19.072 --> 00:01:20.470
How long did it take?

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:26.486
<v><b>Jo:</b></v> I did a ‘spider phobia’ course, it was a one-day course at London Zoo.

00:01:27.083 --> 00:01:31.056
Eh, we were a group of about 15 people.

00:01:31.566 --> 00:01:34.235
First there was a session with a doctor.

00:01:34.510 --> 00:01:39.392
We learned a lot of facts about spiders, and talked about what we were afraid of,

00:01:39.922 --> 00:01:42.160
and we did a hypnotherapy session.

00:01:42.582 --> 00:01:44.599
Then we went to the spider house.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:49.106
The other people on the course went up close to the glass to look at the spiders,

00:01:49.358 --> 00:01:52.830
and they were saying, ‘Ah I’m cured, I feel fine’.

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:58.732
But I stayed at the back of the group, and I was crying because I was still terrified.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:04.497
But a bit later I was able to pick up a small spider with a piece of paper

00:02:04.521 --> 00:02:07.823
and a glass over the top of it and walk across the room.

00:02:08.749 --> 00:02:13.361
And by the end of the day, I could hold a tarantula, which was amazing.

00:02:14.037 --> 00:02:16.145
<v><b>Interviewer:</b></v> Do you still have the phobia now?

00:02:16.452 --> 00:02:23.299
<v><b>Jo:</b></v> Well, yes I do, but now if I see one, I am more logical about it,

00:02:23.571 --> 00:02:29.501
my first reaction is to be frightened, but then with a little bit of talking to myself,

00:02:29.891 --> 00:02:33.667
and if it’s not too big, I can usually deal with it.